WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:14.779
- So what do we have?

00:00:21.557 --> 00:00:23.724
- I'm sorry, I'm so sorry.

00:00:30.824 --> 00:00:32.156
- White male, 20's,

00:00:32.156 --> 00:00:34.756
dropping the N-word in
front of his co-workers.

00:00:34.756 --> 00:00:37.192
- Thompson, it is our duty

00:00:37.192 --> 00:00:41.359
to stop these racist mishaps
before they take place.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.023
Bring him in.

00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:47.945
- Is that a...

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.407
Is that a chocolate cigar?

00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:53.716
- Yeah.

00:00:58.882 --> 00:01:00.408
- Captain, you wanted to see me?

00:01:00.408 --> 00:01:03.195
- Joe, what the hell took you so long?

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:04.378
- I was in the bathroom.

00:01:04.378 --> 00:01:08.545
- Sorry, I told myself that
I would stop yelling so much.

00:01:09.811 --> 00:01:13.242
Joseph, meet your new
partner, Detective Albert.

00:01:13.242 --> 00:01:14.665
She's very impressive.

00:01:14.665 --> 00:01:16.626
Top marks at the academy,

00:01:16.626 --> 00:01:18.298
first in her class in--

00:01:18.298 --> 00:01:19.823
- Sir.

00:01:19.823 --> 00:01:21.862
You know I don't need a partner.

00:01:21.862 --> 00:01:23.407
I do my best work alone.

00:01:23.407 --> 00:01:24.990
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:01:26.481 --> 00:01:30.093
- Well that is not an option, Joe!

00:01:30.093 --> 00:01:32.263
I need you to have backup.

00:01:32.263 --> 00:01:34.285
Let's not forget about
the rampant appropriation

00:01:34.285 --> 00:01:36.535
that was October 29th 1989.

00:01:37.599 --> 00:01:39.745
The darkest Diwali.

00:01:39.745 --> 00:01:42.828
Too many sorries, not enough sorries.

00:01:44.635 --> 00:01:48.135
Alright rook, let's see how long you last.

00:01:49.465 --> 00:01:50.867
This is the red room,

00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:52.832
where we receive all of our assignments.

00:01:52.832 --> 00:01:53.665
And this is--

00:01:53.665 --> 00:01:55.217
- This must be the
Oracle who can see people

00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:59.050
do racist things before
they actually do them.

00:02:00.716 --> 00:02:03.120
- That's a lucky guess.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.440
We inform the minority bureau,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.829
based off of the Oracle's premonitions.

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:09.945
We bring the culprits in
front of Lady Justice.

00:02:09.945 --> 00:02:11.612
- So we arrest them.

00:02:13.638 --> 00:02:14.625
- Sort of.

00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:17.661
We more so just give 'em like a...

00:02:17.661 --> 00:02:19.328
Firm talking to, so.

00:02:20.792 --> 00:02:22.057
(water splashing)

00:02:22.057 --> 00:02:24.391
(gasping)

00:02:24.391 --> 00:02:25.557
- How long was I under for?

00:02:25.557 --> 00:02:26.422
- A minute thirty.

00:02:26.422 --> 00:02:27.397
- Nice, new record.

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:28.230
- Yep.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.084
- Hey Joseph.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:34.875
Alright, Caucasian male
at Theodore Paper Inc,

00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:36.549
10 miles east from here.

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:37.382
- Cool.

00:02:37.382 --> 00:02:38.292
We'll grab a late lunch,

00:02:38.292 --> 00:02:39.140
and then we'll head there.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.390
- Wait, what time did this crime occur?

00:02:44.433 --> 00:02:45.266
- 1:30.

00:02:47.213 --> 00:02:50.213
- Shit, we gotta move, Rook.

00:02:50.213 --> 00:02:51.285
(horn honking)

00:02:51.285 --> 00:02:52.202
Move, move!

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.186
- Take a left up here.

00:02:55.186 --> 00:02:56.271
(tires squealing)

00:02:56.271 --> 00:02:57.259
No, a right, a right.

00:02:57.259 --> 00:03:00.009
- God dammit, Rook, this is
a life or death situation.

00:03:00.009 --> 00:03:03.009
(rap music playing)

00:03:06.454 --> 00:03:07.287
- What time is it?

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.537
- I don't know.

00:03:20.747 --> 00:03:23.330
- I'm just like "Wattup my sh--

00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:27.000
What the hell are you doing?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.381
- Sir, I'm going to need you to slowly

00:03:28.381 --> 00:03:30.963
step away from your co-workers.

00:03:30.963 --> 00:03:31.953
- What's going on?

00:03:31.953 --> 00:03:32.786
- Sir, what you were about to say

00:03:32.786 --> 00:03:34.445
is not permitted by your race.

00:03:34.445 --> 00:03:35.501
- Oh come on, but these--

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:36.615
- Stop, please don't do this.

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:37.969
You're hurting more than you're helping.

00:03:37.969 --> 00:03:38.802
- But what if I--

00:03:38.802 --> 00:03:39.635
- No.

00:03:39.635 --> 00:03:40.552
- Or if I--

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:41.385
- No.

00:03:41.385 --> 00:03:42.218
- What if there's a rap song,

00:03:42.218 --> 00:03:43.169
and I'm rappin' along and I--

00:03:43.169 --> 00:03:47.336
- [Coworker] I swear to god,
I'm gonna beat your ass.

00:03:51.105 --> 00:03:52.772
- Okay, yeah, uhm...

00:03:53.895 --> 00:03:56.974
I am so incredibly sorry, I just...

00:03:56.974 --> 00:03:59.607
I think I really admire you guys,

00:03:59.607 --> 00:04:00.997
and I think you're super cool.

00:04:00.997 --> 00:04:03.591
And deep down I wanted to feel cool too,

00:04:03.591 --> 00:04:06.175
and so that was wrong.

00:04:06.175 --> 00:04:07.289
- Hey man,

00:04:07.289 --> 00:04:09.658
you know what's cool?

00:04:09.658 --> 00:04:11.173
- My personality?

00:04:11.173 --> 00:04:12.744
- No.

00:04:12.744 --> 00:04:14.494
Not getting swung on.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.163
- Oh.

00:04:16.163 --> 00:04:18.532
- Plus we know you'll get
fired if you do say it, so.

00:04:18.532 --> 00:04:19.365
- Wait, what?

00:04:19.365 --> 00:04:20.198
- Thank you.

00:04:20.198 --> 00:04:21.803
(applauding)

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:24.053
- We're just doing our job.

00:04:25.413 --> 00:04:27.939
- Am I really getting fired?

00:04:27.939 --> 00:04:29.522
Hey, what's up man?

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.335
- That was a good one-two back there.

00:04:32.335 --> 00:04:33.571
- Don't get cocky.

00:04:33.571 --> 00:04:35.452
Usually that last one doesn't
get through to people,

00:04:35.452 --> 00:04:36.727
until a few hours of arguing,

00:04:36.727 --> 00:04:39.754
and two plays of To Pimp a Butterfly.

00:04:39.754 --> 00:04:41.797
- So it doesn't get easier from here.

00:04:41.797 --> 00:04:42.880
- It doesn't.

00:04:44.415 --> 00:04:46.248
But you'll get better.

00:04:47.392 --> 00:04:48.489
Come on partner.

00:04:48.489 --> 00:04:51.039
I got a two-for-one deal
at the Cheesecake Factory.

00:04:51.039 --> 00:04:52.908
- [Dispatcher On Radio] Calling
all cars, calling all cars.

00:04:52.908 --> 00:04:55.371
We've got a young woman
wearing a Native American

00:04:55.371 --> 00:04:57.878
head dress at Coachella, over.

00:04:57.878 --> 00:04:58.790
- Rain check?

00:04:58.790 --> 00:04:59.873
- Rain check.

00:05:08.945 --> 00:05:12.112
(soft ballad playing)

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:27.592
(indistinct rapping)

